&lt;/a>
&lt;img src="https://img.shields.io/github/languages/top/dewiweb/clock_X_overlay?style=flat-square&amp;color=f59e0b&amp;labelColor=1e1e2e" alt="true" />
&lt;/div>
&lt;h2>Overview&lt;span class="hx-absolute -hx-mt-20" id="overview">&lt;/span>
&lt;a href="#overview" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section">&lt;/a>&lt;/h2>&lt;p>&lt;strong>Always-on-top OSD clock for Linux X11&lt;/strong> — the control-room tool that keeps the time visible on any workstation, above every window. Configurable, lightweight, universal.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2>Features&lt;span class="hx-absolute -hx-mt-20" id="features">&lt;/span>
&lt;a href="#features" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section">&lt;/a>&lt;/h2>&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Displays above all windows (OSD overlay)&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Click-through&lt;/strong>: the mouse passes through the clock&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Draggable, system tray icon&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Full settings: font, size, colors, opacity, strftime format, position (9 zones), screen selection&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Real-time preview, persistent configuration&lt;/li>
